# An agent's filesystem write tool takes the target path out of the tool
# arguments -- `args.get("path")` -- resolves it against a workspace root and
# re-validates it, then creates the missing parent directories and writes the
# file (src/tools/filesystem.rs `WriteFileTool::execute` at the parent of the
# fix). Every one of those steps addresses the path by name: the containment
# walk skips components that do not exist yet, `create_dir_all` materialises
# them by following whatever appears there, and `tokio::fs::write` opens the
# final component following whatever it points at. The validation therefore
# binds a resolution the mutation does not use: a dangling symlink planted at a
# component the walk skipped, a link swapped into the window between the check
# and the open, or a hard link aliased to an inode outside the root all write
# outside the workspace. The hard-link count is read before the open rather
# than from the open handle, so it can be invalidated the same way.
#
# The fixed revision moves the mutation into a helper that walks the chain one component
# at a time, re-inspecting with `symlink_metadata` and re-comparing after each
# creation, opens with `libc::O_NOFOLLOW`, and reads `nlink()` off the
# open handle. The write tool keeps no by-name creation or write call of its
# own, which is what the reject cases model: the anchored form, and the two
# halves of the anchor (a no-follow open, an lstat of the final component)
# each taken alone.
#
# The binding keys on the documented halves of the shape and nothing else: a
# path field read out of a parsed value (`Value::get` on a `"path"` key), a
# by-name creation or write in the same function (`fs::write`,
# `fs::create_dir_all`, `File::create`, `write_all`), and no link-anchored
# primitive (`O_NOFOLLOW`, `symlink_metadata`/`lstat`, `read_link`, `nlink`,
# `create_new`/`O_EXCL`, an `openat`/dirfd-relative open). A resolved path is
# the ordinary way to write application-owned files -- `persist_state` in
# providers/quota.rs and `save` in tools/reminder.rs build the same
# create-parents-then-write sequence at a path the process chose itself -- so
# the caller-supplied field read is the clause that separates the boundary
# from the idiom, and it is function-confined.
#
# Measured on both revisions of the tree, three `--cache off` runs each: the
# parent reports the finding at tools/filesystem.rs:186
# (`WriteFileTool::execute`) and tools/filesystem.rs:433
# (`EditFileTool::execute`), the fixed revision reports zero, and the rest of the tree is
# unchanged. Across the twelve rust clones under the pool that carry
# `create_dir_all`, an exhaustive grep finds the payload-read-plus-write
# conjunction in three further files, and each is a read tool whose `write`
# calls live in its test module -- no function-level match outside this
# repository.

test "rank1993: a write tool takes the path from the tool arguments and creates the chain and the file by name"
  lang rust
  expect VYQL-PATH-088
  expect_review code.PayloadPathWriteWithoutNoFollow
  code
  ```
  use async_trait::async_trait;
  use serde_json::Value;
  use std::path::Path;

  use crate::error::{Result, ZeptoError};
  use crate::security::{check_hardlink_write, revalidate_path, validate_path_in_workspace};

  use super::{Tool, ToolContext, ToolOutput};

  fn resolve_path(path: &str, ctx: &ToolContext) -> Result<(String, String)> {
      let workspace = ctx.workspace.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| {
          ZeptoError::SecurityViolation("Workspace not configured".to_string())
      })?;
      let safe_path = validate_path_in_workspace(path, workspace)?;
      Ok((safe_path.as_path().to_string_lossy().to_string(), workspace.clone()))
  }

  pub struct WriteFileTool;

  #[async_trait]
  impl Tool for WriteFileTool {
      async fn execute(&self, args: Value, ctx: &ToolContext) -> Result<ToolOutput> {
          let path = args
              .get("path")
              .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
              .ok_or_else(|| ZeptoError::Tool("Missing 'path' argument".into()))?;

          let content = args
              .get("content")
              .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
              .ok_or_else(|| ZeptoError::Tool("Missing 'content' argument".into()))?;

          let (full_path, workspace) = resolve_path(path, ctx)?;
          let full_path_ref = Path::new(&full_path);

          // TOCTOU: re-validate BEFORE any filesystem mutation (including mkdir)
          revalidate_path(full_path_ref, &workspace)?;

          // Create parent directories if they don't exist
          if let Some(parent) = full_path_ref.parent() {
              if !parent.as_os_str().is_empty() {
                  tokio::fs::create_dir_all(parent).await.map_err(|e| {
                      ZeptoError::Tool(format!("Failed to create parent directories: {}", e))
                  })?;
              }
          }

          // Hardlink check: block writes to files with multiple hard links
          check_hardlink_write(full_path_ref)?;

          tokio::fs::write(&full_path, content).await.map_err(|e| {
              ZeptoError::Tool(format!("Failed to write file '{}': {}", full_path, e))
          })?;

          Ok(ToolOutput::llm_only(format!("Successfully wrote {}", full_path)))
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1993: the write opens the resolved path with a no-follow flag and reads the link count off the open handle"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-PATH-088
  reject_review code.PayloadPathWriteWithoutNoFollow
  code
  ```
  use serde_json::Value;
  use std::path::Path;

  #[cfg(unix)]
  use std::{fs::OpenOptions, io::Write as _, os::unix::fs::MetadataExt, os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt};

  use crate::error::{Result, ZeptoError};
  use crate::security::{ensure_directory_chain_secure, revalidate_path, validate_path_in_workspace};

  fn resolve_path(path: &str, workspace: &str) -> Result<String> {
      let safe_path = validate_path_in_workspace(path, workspace)?;
      Ok(safe_path.as_path().to_string_lossy().to_string())
  }

  #[cfg(unix)]
  fn write_file_secure_blocking(path: &Path, workspace: &str, content: &[u8]) -> Result<()> {
      if let Some(parent) = path.parent() {
          if !parent.as_os_str().is_empty() {
              ensure_directory_chain_secure(parent, workspace)?;
              revalidate_path(parent, workspace)?;
          }
      }

      revalidate_path(path, workspace)?;

      let mut options = OpenOptions::new();
      options
          .write(true)
          .create(true)
          .custom_flags(libc::O_NOFOLLOW);
      let mut file = options.open(path).map_err(|e| {
          ZeptoError::Tool(format!("Failed to securely open file '{}': {}", path.display(), e))
      })?;

      let metadata = file.metadata().map_err(|e| {
          ZeptoError::Tool(format!("Failed to inspect opened file '{}': {}", path.display(), e))
      })?;
      if metadata.is_file() && metadata.nlink() > 1 {
          return Err(ZeptoError::SecurityViolation(format!(
              "Write blocked: '{}' has {} hard links and may alias content outside workspace",
              path.display(),
              metadata.nlink()
          )));
      }

      file.set_len(0).map_err(|e| {
          ZeptoError::Tool(format!("Failed to truncate file '{}': {}", path.display(), e))
      })?;
      file.write_all(content).map_err(|e| {
          ZeptoError::Tool(format!("Failed to write file '{}': {}", path.display(), e))
      })?;

      Ok(())
  }

  pub struct WriteFileTool;

  #[async_trait::async_trait]
  impl WriteFileTool {
      pub async fn execute(&self, args: Value, ctx: &crate::tools::ToolContext) -> Result<crate::tools::ToolOutput> {
          let path = args
              .get("path")
              .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
              .ok_or_else(|| ZeptoError::Tool("Missing 'path' argument".into()))?;

          let content = args
              .get("content")
              .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
              .ok_or_else(|| ZeptoError::Tool("Missing 'content' argument".into()))?;

          let full_path = resolve_path(path, ctx.workspace.as_deref().ok_or_else(|| {
              ZeptoError::SecurityViolation("Workspace not configured".to_string())
          })?)?;

          write_file_secure_blocking(Path::new(&full_path), "workspace", content.as_bytes())?;

          Ok(crate::tools::ToolOutput::llm_only(format!("Successfully wrote {}", full_path)))
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1993: a process-owned path written the same way is the ordinary save idiom"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-PATH-088
  reject_review code.PayloadPathWriteWithoutNoFollow
  code
  ```
  use std::collections::HashMap;
  use std::path::Path;

  fn persist_state(path: &Path, state: &HashMap<String, u32>) {
      if let Some(parent) = path.parent() {
          if let Err(e) = std::fs::create_dir_all(parent) {
              eprintln!("failed to create dir {}: {}", parent.display(), e);
              return;
          }
      }
      match serde_json::to_string_pretty(state) {
          Ok(json) => {
              if let Err(e) = std::fs::write(path, &json) {
                  eprintln!("failed to write state to {}: {}", path.display(), e);
              }
          }
          Err(e) => eprintln!("failed to serialise state: {}", e),
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1993: inspecting the final component with lstat before writing leaves no link to follow blindly"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-PATH-088
  reject_review code.PayloadPathWriteWithoutNoFollow
  code
  ```
  use serde_json::Value;
  use std::path::Path;

  fn write_args_file(args: &Value, workspace: &str) -> std::io::Result<()> {
      let path = args.get("path").and_then(|v| v.as_str()).ok_or_else(|| {
          std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput, "missing path")
      })?;
      let full = Path::new(workspace).join(path);

      match std::fs::symlink_metadata(&full) {
          Ok(meta) if meta.file_type().is_symlink() => {
              return Err(std::io::Error::new(
                  std::io::ErrorKind::PermissionDenied,
                  "refusing to follow a link at the target",
              ));
          }
          _ => {}
      }

      if let Some(parent) = full.parent() {
          std::fs::create_dir_all(parent)?;
      }
      std::fs::write(&full, "data")
  }
  ```
